#%PAM-1.0
#
# The greeter's *own* session: greetd starting wlrix-greeter as the wlrix-greeter system
# account, before anybody has logged in. Named by `[default_session] service` in
# wlrix-greeter.toml.
#
# Shipped rather than left to greetd's default of `greetd-greeter`, which no distribution is
# obliged to provide -- Arch's greetd package ships only `greetd`, and PAM's fallback for an
# unknown service is `other`, which denies everything. The greeter would not start at all.

# No password to check: this is a system account with no login of its own.
auth       required     pam_permit.so

account    include      system-login

session    include      system-login
